* Sat Sep 26 2026 Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com> - 2.0.0-1
- Ships the patch instead of the patched binary. The single byte at 0x2c061 is
  now applied to the copy in the user's own vendor.img at reconcile time,
  between a check of the stock hash and a check of the result, so this package
  no longer redistributes Waydroid's vendor binary (docs/54). The bytes were
  always already on any machine that could run this.
- Major version because the payload shape changed, not the effect: the file that
  lands in the overlay is byte-identical to what 1.0.0 shipped, which is
  asserted by bin/overlay-sync-test.sh against the copy in this repository.
- Requires waydroid-ext-overlay-sync >= 1.1.0, which is where derive rows are
  understood. An older reconciler would fail loudly rather than deploy nothing,
  but the dependency means it cannot get that far.
- The resolution-cap XML stays a plain payload row: it is text produced by
  deleting lines from the stock file, which is ours to ship. Its stock hash is
  now recorded as a bare sha256 rather than by naming a copy of the file.

* Thu Sep 24 2026 Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com> - 1.0.0-1
- First package. Closes the last unsatisfiable dependency of the camera group
  together with the retirement of waydroid-ext-uvc-autosuspend (docs/12).
- Requires waydroid-ext-camera-gbm rather than recommending it: this package
  only makes more apps willing to open a camera whose frames are black without
  that one.
- The resolution cap is stated in the description, not just in a comment. It
  costs a 1080p-capable camera its top mode and that is not a detail to bury.
